                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "syndactyly",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "perform at ~ 1 year of age",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "acrosyndactyly",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "perform in neonatal period",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Digit Release**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "if multiple digits are involved perform procedure in **two stages (do 1 side of a finger at a time)** to avoid compromising vasculature",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "release digits with significant length differences first to avoid growth disturbances",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "release border digits first (ring-little, and thumb-index) at <6mths because of differential growth rates between ring-little and between thumb-index digits",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "middle-ring syndactyly can be released later (2yr old) as because middle and ring digits have similar growth rates",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "thus if syndactyly involving index-middle and ring-small digits, release index-middle and ring-small first, and leave the central syndactyly (middle-ring) for 6 months later",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "do all releases before school age",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "bilateral hand releases",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "perform simultaneously if child is <18mths (less active)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "perform staged if child is >18mths (more active, hard to immobilize bilateral limbs simultaneously)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**interdigitating zigzag flaps** are created during release to avoid longitudinal scarring",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6076/images/zig%20zag.jpg",
                  "caption": "Zigzag technique"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "dorsal fasciocutaneous flaps to reconstruct the web",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "use only absorbable sutures (5-0 chromic catgut) which have less inflammation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Web creep**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6076/images/48bc940b-7558-4d0e-80dd-0b75027d953c_web_creep..jpg",
              "caption": "Web creep"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common complication of surgical treatment (8-60%)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "causes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**early** creep is most commonly caused by necrosis of the tip of the dorsal quadrilateral flap and loss of full-thickness skin graft placed in the web",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**late** creep (adolescence) is caused by discrepant growth between scar/skin graft and surrounding tissue during the growth spurt",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "reconstruct web space with local skin flaps",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Nail deformities**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
